        <p class="sr-only">
          Four sample stories with Lee Flooring. Business: the owner, Sam, sets up the business by text: the kinds of
          work, the business card, an ID check, an optional license, services and prices with a measure visit, what is
          taken at booking, hours and rules, About us and photos, the Rosfield fee, then Go live and three team members.
          Customer: Maya books a measure visit. Rosie checks the place first, asks only what sets the price, offers
          arrival times, asks the flooring questions (the year the home was built, furniture, slab or crawl space, own or
          rent), explains the glue test and that pianos need a mover, takes the street address on a secure page, books
          it with a check-in code and a calendar card, and the owner gets a notice. Team: Danny, the estimator, joins
          from the invite, adds the job to his calendar, gets his day list, checks in with the code, sends his notes and
          a quote that goes to Sam first because it is over 500 dollars. Website: an AI assistant books for Maya on
          rosfield.com; Rosie keeps the business's price, never takes a door code through an AI, and Maya confirms the
          booking herself.
        </p>
